    "processing_note": "Processed by wetterdienst: the provider's data was reshaped into a uniform table, and its units converted where they differ. The annual values were calculated from the provider's daily values by the rules of WMO-No. 1203: a day is the midrange of TMAX and TMIN, which is no 24-hour mean, used for every day so that the method does not change along the record (TAVG is not used); a month counts with at most 10 days missing and at most 4 in a row, and a year with all 12 months counting is the mean of its monthly means; a year that fails is a gap. The anomaly and class of each year were calculated from the annual values calculated above: the mean of 1971-2000 is the centre and the scale spans +/-2.6 standard deviations of 1901-2000 in 16 classes (Hawkins' method).",
